### **6. ASSESSMENT: NET NEW WORK FOR SHARED FOLDER BATCH + DRAG-MOVE**

| Component | Private-Vault | Shared-Folder | Reusable? | Effort |
|-----------|---------------|---------------|-----------|--------|
| **Selection state** | ✓ `selectedIds` Set in useFileBrowserActions | ✗ Absent | Partial (copy pattern, rename hook) | LOW |
| **Batch move dialog state** | ✓ `batchMoveDialog` in useFileBrowserActions | ✗ Absent | Direct copy | MINIMAL |
| **MoveDialog component** | ✓ Flexible (item + items props) | ✗ Not used | Full reuse if mounted | MINIMAL |
| **Batch move handler** | ✓ `handleBatchMoveClick`, `handleBatchMoveConfirm` | ✗ Absent | Adapted copy (different write op hook) | LOW |
| **Drag source** | ✓ FileListItem.handleDragStart + multi-select payload | ✗ SharedFolderRow has no drag | Copy with SharedFolderRow integration | LOW |
| **Drop handler** | ✓ FileListItem.handleDrop + folder target logic | ✗ SharedFolderRow has no drop | Copy with SharedFolderRow integration | LOW |
| **useFileBrowserActions flow** | ✓ handleDropOnFolder → moveItem/moveItems | ✗ No equivalent hook | Create `useSharedFileBrowserActions` mirror | MEDIUM |
| **SDK moveInSharedFolder** | ✗ Not needed (uses own vault moveItem) | ✗ **MUST CREATE** | N/A (net new) | **HIGH** |
| **SDK batch loop** | ✓ Loops moveItem in web layer (useFolderMutations) | ✓ Mirror approach possible | Use same pattern | MINIMAL |

